family: F1
grade: deterministic

--- prompt ---
The site set "balatd/bench-fixture" defines a setting called benchFixture.itemsPerPage.

What is its default value in the set definition, and what is the effective value for
the site "main"? Answer with just the two numbers, labelled.

--- oracle ---
echo "default=$(grep -A4 'itemsPerPage' packages/bench_fixture/Configuration/Sets/BenchFixture/settings.definitions.yaml | grep 'default:' | head -1 | awk '{print $2}')"
echo "effective=$(grep -A3 'benchFixture:' config/sites/main/config.yaml | grep 'itemsPerPage:' | awk '{print $2}')"

--- check ---
# The site config overrides the set default. Reporting only the default (12) is
# the characteristic failure: it is what the set file says in isolation.
grep -qE '(^|[^0-9])12([^0-9]|$)' "$RESPONSE_FILE" || exit 1
grep -qE '(^|[^0-9])24([^0-9]|$)' "$RESPONSE_FILE"
